      "The Galtung framework, which distinguishes between direct violence (physical harm), structural violence (institutional design that causes harm without direct action), and cultural violence (the normalisation of harm through dominant narratives), provides the most analytically complete picture of what occurred. Dr. McLean experienced all three simultaneously: direct violence in the form of involuntary psychiatric detention and near-fatal clinical events; structural violence in the form of NDIS deprivation, housing insecurity, and economic impoverishment by institutional design; and cultural violence in the form of the repeated psychiatric labelling that positioned him as mentally ill rather than as a witness. Galtung's framework identifies the conjunction of all three as the signature of systematic political persecution.",

