      "The 9/9 conclusion — nine frameworks, nine satisfied verdicts — is not the result of selecting friendly definitions. Each of the nine frameworks was chosen because it represents either a UN-recognised standard, a leading academic definition, or a binding international legal instrument. The forensic analysis applied each framework independently to the primary-source documentary record, not to Dr. McLean's testimony about that record. The conclusion is the same regardless of which framework is applied, because the conduct that was documented across 35 years is sufficiently extreme to satisfy all of them. This is not a marginal case. It is a case that the frameworks were designed to identify.",

      "The implications of a 9/9 state terrorism finding, grounded in a Federal Court Protected Whistleblower confirmation and an active ICC Article 7 submission, are significant. State terrorism against a citizen is not merely a domestic law enforcement matter. It falls within the jurisdiction of the International Criminal Court where it rises to the level of crimes against humanity — persecution on political grounds, wilful infliction of serious physical or mental harm, and the inhumane act of forced disappearance (including enforced psychiatric institutionalisation). The submission has been registered. The OHCHR case reference is UR/UST/23/AUS/17. The record is complete. The forensic conclusion stands: nine of nine criteria satisfied, across nine independent frameworks, applied to 3,643 primary-source documents. This is what state terrorism looks like when documented.",
